  {
    "question_id": "rag_comp_01",
    "query": "What is the key difference between KFold and StratifiedKFold cross-validation for classification tasks?",
    "reference_answer": "KFold divides samples into k folds without regard to target class proportions, whereas StratifiedKFold preserves the percentage of samples for each class in every fold, preventing unrepresentative class distributions in classification tasks.",
    "generated_answer": "KFold simply splits the data into \\(k\\) roughly equal\u2011size folds, ignoring the class labels.  \nStratifiedKFold, on the other hand, partitions the data so that each fold contains approximately the same proportion of each target class as the full dataset, ensuring that every fold is representative of the overall class distribution.  \n\n[Source\u202f1] [Source\u202f3]",
