  {
    "question_id": "rag_multi_09",
    "query": "How do preprocessing, pipelines, and model selection work together to build leak-free machine learning workflows in scikit-learn?",
    "reference_answer": "Preprocessing transformers (scalers, encoders, imputers) and models are chained in a Pipeline, and the entire pipeline is passed to model selection tools (GridSearchCV or cross_val_score); this ensures preprocessing parameters are estimated solely on training splits, eliminating data leakage.",
    "generated_answer": "Preprocessing, pipelines, and model\u2011selection tools in scikit\u2011learn are designed to keep the training and test data completely separate, so that no information from the test set can influence the model.\n\n1. **Pre\u2011processing must be learned only on the training data**  \n   * Fit\u2011methods (`fit`, `fit_transform`) should never be called on the full dataset or on the test split.  \n   * The same transformation must then be applied to the test data with `transform` (or `fit_transform` on the training set followed by `transform` on the test set) [Source\u202f1, Source\u202f2].\n\n2. **Pipelines enforce the correct order of operations**  \n   * A `Pipeline` chains transformers and a final estimator.  \n   * All intermediate steps implement `fit` and `transform`; the last step only needs `fit`.  \n   * When the pipeline is fitted, each transformer is fitted on the training data only, and the same fitted transformers are used to transform the test data automatically.  \n   * Pipelines also make it easy to include the entire preprocessing + model in cross\u2011validation or hyper\u2011parameter search, preventing accidental leakage of test data into the training process [Source\u202f3, Source\u202f4].\n\n3. **Model selection (cross\u2011validation, grid search, etc.) should be performed on the pipeline**  \n   * By passing the pipeline to `cross_val_score`, `GridSearchCV`, or `RandomizedSearchCV`, the entire preprocessing + estimator chain is evaluated on each fold, ensuring that each fold\u2019s training data is used to fit the transformers and the estimator, and the fold\u2019s test data is only used for scoring.  \n   * This keeps the test data out of the fitting process and yields realistic performance estimates [Source\u202f5].\n\nIn short, fit all preprocessing steps on the training split, wrap them together with the estimator in a `Pipeline`, and run any cross\u2011validation or hyper\u2011parameter tuning on that pipeline. This workflow guarantees that the test data never influences the learned parameters, thereby preventing data leakage.",
