  {
    "question_id": "rag_multi_09",
    "query": "How do preprocessing, pipelines, and model selection work together to build leak-free machine learning workflows in scikit-learn?",
    "reference_answer": "Preprocessing transformers (scalers, encoders, imputers) and models are chained in a Pipeline, and the entire pipeline is passed to model selection tools (GridSearchCV or cross_val_score); this ensures preprocessing parameters are estimated solely on training splits, eliminating data leakage.",
    "generated_answer": "Preprocessing, pipelines, and model\u2011selection tools in scikit\u2011learn are designed to keep the statistics that are learned from the data (means, variances, feature\u2011selection masks, etc.) **only** from the training portion of the data.  The same fitted transformers are then applied to the test or validation data, which guarantees that no information from the test set leaks into the model.\n\n| Step | What happens | Why it prevents leakage |\n|------|--------------|------------------------|\n| **Split first** | `train_test_split` (or a CV splitter) is called before any preprocessing. | The test set is never seen by any transformer. |\n| **Fit on training data** | `fit` or `fit_transform` is called only on the training split. | The transformer learns statistics (e.g., mean, std, selected features) solely from the training data. |\n| **Transform test data** | `transform` (or `fit_transform` on the training split, then `transform` on the test split) is used. | The same transformation is applied to the test data without re\u2011learning any statistics. |\n| **Pipeline** | A `Pipeline` chains the preprocessing steps and the final estimator. | The pipeline\u2019s `fit` method automatically calls `fit` on each transformer in order, then `transform` on all but the last step, and finally `fit` on the estimator.  This guarantees that each step is applied only to the data that has already been processed by the previous steps, and that the test data is never used to fit any transformer. |\n| **Cross\u2011validation / hyper\u2011parameter search** | `GridSearchCV`, `RandomizedSearchCV`, or `cross_val_score` are run on the pipeline. | During each CV fold the pipeline is re\u2011fitted on the training fold only; the validation fold is transformed with the fitted pipeline, so no leakage occurs. |\n| **ColumnTransformer** | Different columns can be processed with different transformers inside a pipeline. | Each transformer is still fitted only on the training data, and the same fitted transformers are applied to the test data. |\n| **StandardScaler example** | `StandardScaler().fit(X_train)` \u2192 `scaler.transform(X_test)`. | The scaler\u2019s mean and std are computed from `X_train` only, then reused for `X_test`. |\n| **Feature selection example** | `SelectKBest(k=25).fit(X_train, y_train)` \u2192 `X_train_sel = selector.transform(X_train)`; `X_test_sel",
