    "question_id": "rag_trouble_07",
    "query": "Why does feature selection with SelectKBest prior to train_test_split cause severe test error underestimation?",
    "reference_answer": "Selecting features using targets from the whole dataset exposes the selector to test labels, selecting spurious features correlated with test targets and causing severe data leakage; feature selection must be fitted only on training folds via Pipeline.",
    "generated_answer": "Feature selection performed **before** splitting the data leaks information from the test set into the training process.  \nWhen `SelectKBest` is fit on the entire dataset, it uses the test labels to rank features, so the chosen features are biased toward patterns that also appear in the test set. Consequently, the model trained on those features will appear to perform much better than it truly will on unseen data, leading to a severe under\u2011estimation of the test error (i.e., an overly optimistic accuracy).  \n\nThis is why the correct practice is to split first, then fit the selector only on the training split, and finally transform the test split with the fitted selector.  \n\n[Source\u202f1] and [Source\u202f2] describe this leakage and its effect on accuracy.",
